# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Jupyter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── DVC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/data/bronze/
/data/silver/
/data/gold/
# Synthetic output of the `smoke` CI wiring target — a DVC out, and not a
# result: it must never be committed or mistaken for an evaluation artifact.
/data/smoke/
# Catch-all. The four lines above enumerate subdirectories, which is exactly how
# `data/interim/` (added 2026-08-08 for the BAM coverage probe) slipped through
# and showed up as untracked. Nothing under data/ is git-tracked — it is all
# DVC-managed — so the safe default is to ignore the tree and let a future
# exception be added deliberately rather than discovered. Findings that belong
# in the record go to docs/, not here.
/data/
*.dvc
# the DVC config directory itself IS tracked (its own .gitignore excludes the cache)
!.dvc

# ── Generated tool output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# graphify knowledge-graph artifacts (~8 MB: cache/, graph.html, graph.json).
# Regenerable from the repo at any time, so versioning them would add weight
# without adding information.
graphify-out/

# ── MLflow ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mlruns/
mlflow/mlflow.db
mlflow/artifacts/

# ── Dagster ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.dagster_home/
.tmp_dagster_home_*/
dagster.yaml

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Environment variables ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env.local

# ── Claude Code ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.v2.md
.claude/

# ── Codex ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AGENTS.md

